{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe audit (ae1b) flagged broad-but-shallow typing: only `rebar.graph.*` / `rebar.grounding.*` are gated at `disallow_untyped_defs` (pyproject.toml). The full ratchet FLIP overlaps pyproject.toml (contended by 9 in-progress tickets) and is therefore OUT of scope here. This story does the NON-overlapping, low-risk prep: fully annotate the self-contained security-focused `attest` package (`attest/*.py`, ~1770 LOC, 7 files) so it is ready to join the ratchet. All attest files have ZERO in-progress contention.\n\n## Plan\n- Annotate remaining function signatures in `src/rebar/attest/*.py` until `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` is clean.\n- Add real, useful annotations. Do NOT reach for `: Any` widening to silence the check: there are exactly TWO pre-existing explicit `Any` annotations today, both on the `trust_root` boundary parameter (`registry.py:62` and `registry.py:89`), which is a genuine externally-supplied verifier trust root. This story must NOT introduce any additional `: Any` (or `-> Any`) annotations to satisfy `disallow_untyped_defs`; the count of explicit `Any` annotations must stay at 2.\n- Do NOT edit pyproject.toml here — the one-line ratchet promotion is a trivial fast-follow to land once pyproject.toml contention clears; track under 06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` reports no errors (proves every def is annotated).\n- [ ] The no-widening constraint is machine-checked, NOT left to manual review: `grep -rnE ':\\s*Any\\b|->\\s*Any\\b' src/rebar/attest/*.py | wc -l` reports **exactly 2** (the pre-existing `trust_root` boundary at `registry.py:62,89`) — i.e. no new `: Any`/`-> Any` was added. (Rationale: `--disallow-untyped-defs` treats an `: Any` signature as fully typed and passes it, so a grep-count is the oracle that actually enforces AC intent.)\n- [ ] Existing gates (normal mypy, lint, tests) remain green; pyproject.toml untouched (verified by `git diff --stat` showing no `pyproject.toml` change).\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches only `src/rebar/attest/*.py` — all free of in-progress contention. The pyproject ratchet flip is explicitly deferred to avoid contention with in-progress tickets."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786223312934937001,"uuid":"1b6742fa-bc6d-4e8e-b68a-61a851a0c870"}